The main goal of this paper is to establish an upper bound on the minimal size of separating formulas, assuming they exist. Our approach does not work with every satisfaction relation, thus we need to assume that it satisfies some conditions. These conditions are met in various use-cases, several of which we detail in Section~\ref{sec:examples}. In this section, we formally define the assumptions that we make on the satisfaction relation; we state the main theorem of this paper and we provide a detailed proof sketch. We then discuss a meta enumeration algorithm solving the passive learning problem derived from the proof of this theorem.

