	Let $\Sigma := \{a,b,c,d,e\}$. For all $n \geq 3$, there is an automaton $A_n$ with $25n+111$ states, a single initial state and such that a smallest word in $\Sigma^*$ that is not accepted by $A_n$ is of size $(2^n-1) \cdot (n+1) +1$.
\end{theorem}

By turning finite automata into Kripke structures, we establish the proposition below.
\begin{proposition}[Proof~\ref{proof:lower_bound_ml}]
