\section{Experiment}\label{sec:exp}
\subsection{Experiment Settings}
\stitle{Datasets.}
We utilize six public vector datasets, which are widely used in benchmarking and evaluation(SIFT GIST)\footnote{https://www.cse.cuhk.edu.hk/systems/hash/gqr/datasets.html}. Some of them are generated by state-of-the-art AI embedding models (MSMARCO\footnote{https://huggingface.co/datasets/Cohere/msmarco-v2.1-embed-english-v3} OpenAI-1536\footnote{https://huggingface.co/datasets/Qdrant/dbpedia-entities-openai3-text-embedding-3-large-1536-1M}  OpenAI-3072\footnote{https://huggingface.co/datasets/Qdrant/dbpedia-entities-openai3-text-embedding-3-large-3072-1M}). For the Label part, except for the paper dataset, which comes with real labels, we use the method of the previous works~\cite{UNG-SIGMOD-2025,Filtered-diskann-WWW-2023} to generate label data with different distributions for other datasets. Note that some datasets have variable vector entries. We randomly sample 1 million vectors as the base vector if the dataset cardinality exceeds 1M. Moreover, we also sampled 100M data from the deep1B\footnote{https://storage.yandexcloud.net/yandex-research/ann-datasets/T2I/base.1B.fbin} dataset to verify the scalability of our algorithms.

