	We consider a cell with radius $50$m including $K=2$ SBSs. Each SBS belongs to a different technology (RAT-1 or -2). The bandwidth and the noise power density are $180$kHz and $-174$dBm/Hz, respectively. The channel gain between the $i$-th user and the $k$-th SBS is expressed as $h_{ik}=\psi d_{ik}^{-3}$ where $d_{ik}$ is the distance between the $i$-th user and the $k$-th SBS and $\psi$ is a Rayleigh random variable with unit variance. The parameters of problem \eqref{RAT-problem} are $	N_{\max}^{(m)}=I-1,  w_{\max}^{(m)}=\underset{i \in \mathcal{I},k \in \mathcal{K}_m}{\max} \ r_{ik},  K^{(k)}_{\max}=I (\forall k), \alpha_i=1 (\forall i)$.

