\begin{abstract}
  We investigate blob-trees,
  a new way of connecting a set of points, by a mixture
  of enclosing them by cycles (as in the convex hull) and
  connecting them by edges (as in a spanning tree).
  We show that a minimum-cost blob-tree
  for $n$ points can be
  computed in $O(n^3)$ time.
\end{abstract}

