We assume that the \iflong point \fi
set $P$ is in general position.
In particular,
\iflong we assume that \fi the pairwise distances between points are unique and no three points are on a line.
This implies that the MST of the point set is %also
unique. We also assume that no two points have the same $x$- or $y$-coordinate.



