Digons are more tricky to define, because they must simultaneously
fulfill the conditions of valid chords and entry or exit walls.
A valid chord
$ab$ with $a\ne r$ is a \defn{valid entry digon} if the
directed edges $uu' \in X^+_{ab}$ satisfy
the following condition:
